maya_sales: Heads-up: CobaltPay POC tomorrow morning. They want streaming SDK + model-initiated synchronous webhook calls (model waits for webhook result), and strict invoice JSON validation at the edge. Also need Hosted vs Dedicated pricing, SOC2 + customer-managed KMS, and option for VPC/IP allowlist. Can someone bring a tiny SDK snippet and a 1-page runbook + a smoke test harness?

rio_devx: On it. Two quick clarifiers: expected peak QPS and avg tokens per response? Are tool/webhook calls single-shot or chained? p50/p95 latency targets?

maya_sales: Peak ~90 QPS, avg ~140 tokens/response. Tool calls ~1/6 responses, single-shot (no nesting). Target p50 <110ms, p95 <300ms. SOC2 + customer KMS mandatory; they prefer traffic from fixed egress IPs (IP allowlist) or VPC peering.

ash_solutions: Pricing note: Hosted = straightforward per-token; Dedicated reserved cluster is better for stable p50 and predictable unit economics at this scale. I'll DM ballpark numbers (hybrid recommendation: reserved baseline + hosted burst).

tess_infra: Security checklist: customer-managed KMS supported (requires onboarding + key policy changes). IP allowlist/VPC -> needs Private deployment or Dedicated with VPC peering and static egress. I'll drop SOC2 attestation PDF in the deal folder. For sync webhooks recommend <1.5s timeouts and client-side circuit-breakers.

rio_devx: Minimal JS snippet (pseudo) for streaming + sync function call + resume:```js
// pseudo example
const rw = new Redwood({ apiKey: process.env.RW_KEY, routing: 'dedicated' });
const stream = rw.stream({ model: 'redwood-rtf-1', streaming: true, functions: [INVOICE_TOOL_SPEC] });
stream.on('chunk', async (c) => {
  if (c.type === 'function_call') {
    // call customer webhook synchronously, timeout ~1500ms
    const res = await fetch(c.webhook, { method: 'POST', body: JSON.stringify(c.args), timeout: 1500 });
    const payload = await res.json();
    // resume streaming with function result
    stream.resumeWithFunctionResult(payload);
  } else {
    process.stdout.write(c.text || '');
  }
});
```

rio_devx: Structured output guidance: require top-level "invoice" object with fields: invoice_id (string), total_cents (number), currency (string), line_items: array of {desc:string, qty:number, unit_cents:number}. Edge validator should reject nonconforming responses and either: a) return structured error to client, or b) route to verification model/human review.

rio_devx: Perf ops tips: use Dedicated routing for stable p50, enable KV prefix caching and prefix hints, batching: max_batch_size=4-8, max_wait_ms=8-12 to balance throughput vs latency. Also set conservative concurrency limits on the webhook worker to avoid head-of-line blocking.

ash_solutions: DMing numbers now. For context, expect a mid-five-figures/month reserved baseline for a small GPU pool; hosted-only could cost more depending on prompt length & usage.

tess_infra: I've uploaded SOC2 PDF + KMS onboarding checklist to the deal folder. Note: for VPC peering we'll need a short network coordination window with their infra team.

rio_devx: I'll assemble a 1-pager runbook + tiny smoke-test harness (node + pytest) and push to presales repo within a few hours. It will include: sample config, schema validator script, mock webhook server, and a simple perf checklist. Ping me for repo invite.

maya_sales: Perfect, scheduling demo 9am. @ash_solutions send the formal quote once you loop finance, @tess_infra thanks for SOC2 drop, @rio_devx ping when runbook is up. :rocket:
